### Does any official UNESCO document use the phrase "most ancient race in the world" in reference to the Nadar community?
Answer: No. The UNESCO 1950 Statement on Race provided in the search result does not mention the Nadar community at all, nor does it use the phrase "most ancient race in the world." In fact, the document explicitly argues against hierarchical classifications of races, stating that "the biological differences between ethnic groups should be disregarded from the standpoint of social acceptance and social action" and emphasizing "the unity of mankind from both the biological and social viewpoints."

